Account Reinitialization Vulnerability Solana Anchor

Reinitialization attack: attacker reinitializes an already-initialized account
to take ownership or reset state, frontrunning the legitimate initializer.

Vulnerable code:
pub fn initialize(ctx: Context<Initialize>) -> Result<()> {
    let account = &mut ctx.accounts.my_account;
    account.owner = ctx.accounts.user.key();
    account.data = 0;
    Ok(())
}

Attack: call initialize() again after victim initializes to steal ownership.

Secure pattern 1 - Anchor init constraint:
#[account(init, payer = user, space = 8 + 32)]
pub my_account: Account<info, MyAccount>

Secure pattern 2 - Manual check:
require!(!account.is_initialized, ErrorCode::AlreadyInitialized);
account.is_initialized = true;

Secure pattern 3 - PDA with seeds prevents reinitialization:
#[account(init, seeds = [b"account", user.key().as_ref()], bump, payer = user, space = 8 + 32)]

Detection: initialize function without init constraint or is_initialized check.
Severity: High — account takeover, fund theft.
Source: Sealevel Attacks program 4-initialization
